Package: sintHiChIP
Title: Accurate HiChIP Interaction Detection Through RE Cut Site Density Modeling
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Weiyue", "Ding", , "wyding0501@hotmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: sintHiChIP detects significant chromatin interactions in HiChIP data 
    by modeling restriction enzyme cut site density as biological signal. 
    Implements dual-mode analysis (local: peak-to-peak; global: genome-wide) 
    with adaptive statistical modeling. Features HiC-Pro integration, numerical 
    stability, and WashU Browser track generation.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: GenomeInfoDb, GenomicRanges, IRanges, Rcpp, S4Vectors,
        data.table, dplyr, matrixStats, methods, readr, stats, tools,
        graphics, MASS
SystemRequirements: bedtools (>= 2.29.0), tabix (>= 1.10), 
                    bgzip (>= 1.10), HiC-Pro (>= 3.1.0)
LinkingTo: Rcpp
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
Suggests: testthat, knitr, rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
NeedsCompilation: yes
URL: https://github.com/wding0501/sintHiChIP
BugReports: https://github.com/wding0501/sintHiChIP/issues
